From 19f277f2602f6710c358aead46dedfa7ecf51e28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bedasrv <bedasrv@warslop-dev>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:36:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: onRoute + onRouteResult re-authored for upstream
 v3.8.53

Replaces the v3.8.52-era patches 0001/0002 and 0007-0011 with a single
v3.8.53-native patch built against upstream v3.8.53 (where the plugin/hook
system was rewritten: emitHook/emitHookBlocking/HookHandler generics,
BUILTIN_EVENTS pinned by plugins-welcome-banner-e2e, decisionTrace and
executeTargetAttempt reworked).

Kept contract, re-implemented:
- onRoute: pre-resolution hook; a plugin's answer (an ordered list of
  model ids) becomes an in-memory priority combo (maxRetries 0) dispatched
  through the existing combo machinery, so per-target policy, cooldowns and
  fallback all apply. Fail-open.
- onRouteResult: one-way notification per dispatched attempt with status
  and allowlisted kind (auth|rate_limit|timeout|provider|model|quality) and
  isUsageLimitError (spent allowance).
- x-omniroute-route/attempts, x-router-reason/confidence/item/specialist/
  thinking on the response head; context_length/max_output_tokens when
  known for the answering attempt.
- earlyStreamKeepalive carries the same provenance in-band when the head
  was committed early (openAiRouteProvenanceFrame on /v1/chat/completions).
- Partial-routing-preserving defaults: unknown windows stay absent, never
  guessed.

Tests: per-route-window, plugins-onroute, earlyStreamKeepalive,
plugins-welcome-banner-e2e; combo suite green (2271 pass), open-sse and
core typecheck clean.
